## Development Log

### Entry 1: 2026-11-18 - Understanding the problem and setting up the project
I started by reading the assignment requirements and understanding that the main problem is Race Condition. I opened the Assignment 1 code and studied how the Ready Queue and CPUs work. I set up the repository on GitHub and made sure the original code runs before any modification, so I have a reference point for comparison.

### Entry 2: 2026-11-20 - Implementing Ready Queue Lock
I added a `ReentrantLock` named `queueLock` in the `ReadyQueue` class. I protected all methods that touch the list and map: `add()`, `poll()`, `processOf()`, and `snapshot()`. I used the pattern `lock()` at the start and `unlock()` in `finally` so the lock is released even if an error happens. I tested the run and confirmed that processes are not lost from the queue.

### Entry 3: 2026-11-22 - Implementing Statistics Lock
I added one lock `statsLock` in the `SharedStats` class to protect the three counters: `contextSwitchCount`, `completedProcessCount`, and `totalServiceTime`. I chose one lock instead of three because the counters are always read together in the verification block, the critical sections are very short, and this avoids deadlock and simplifies the code. After this, the verification results matched the expected values.

### Entry 4: 2026-11-24 - Replacing Busy-Waiting with Semaphore
I added `Semaphore readyCount = new Semaphore(0)` in `ReadyQueue`. In `add()` I call `release()` after releasing the lock, and in `CpuWorker` I call `acquire()` before taking a process. Now the CPU sleeps instead of spinning. I also added `releaseAllForShutdown()` to wake up all CPUs at the end so they terminate cleanly without hanging forever.

### Entry 5: 2026-11-25 - Testing and Final Verification
I ran the program several times and confirmed the verification is all correct: `Context switches`, `Completed processes`, and `Total service time` match, and `Busy-waiting polls = 0`. I recorded the demo video explaining the three features and showing the run in the IDE, then pushed all changes to GitHub.

